## cmesh BYOL hardening — /etc/audit/rules.d/60-cmesh-phi.rules
##
## Access to protected health information. HIPAA wants a record of who READ it, not
## only who changed it. Point these at wherever the application keeps PHI (a database
## directory, an uploads tree, a mount). The defaults watch /srv and /home for writes
## and attribute changes only; a read watch (-p r) on a busy directory is a firehose,
## so add it per directory once you know the volume.
##
## Examples:
##   -w /srv/app/uploads -p rwa -k phi
##   -w /var/lib/postgres/data -p wa -k phi
-w /srv/ -p wa -k phi
-w /home/ -p wa -k phi
